# ACT 2
("tow:gibraltar", "Morehouse decides to sail the Mary Celeste to Gibraltar, with just three of his men, and claim a salvage reward. That's when the questions really begin."),
("court:gibraltar", "In Gibraltar, a hearing is held. The British official leading it is the attorney general, Frederick Solly-Flood. And he is suspicious of everyone."),
("char:think|pirate", "His first idea? Mutiny. Maybe the crew got into the alcohol, got drunk, attacked the captain and his family, and escaped."),
("sword:stains", "He points to marks on the ship's rail, and a sword with stains on it. It sounds dramatic. But when the stains were tested, they were found not to be blood."),
