("book:doyle", "And here's where the legend really grows. In 1884, a young doctor writes a short story about the ship. His name is Arthur Conan Doyle. The man who would later create Sherlock Holmes."),
("book:marie", "In his story he calls it the Marie Celeste, and he invents dramatic details. A ship found in perfect order, with everything just left behind."),
("tea:cup", "Over the years, retellings added things like warm cups of tea on the table and half-eaten breakfasts. Those details are fiction. They were never in the real reports."),
("char:point|book", "But people believed the story. Even today, many people still call her the Marie Celeste. The myth became more famous than the facts."),
("char:think|q", "So if we remove the made-up parts, what's left? A ship with water in its hold, a pump taken apart, a missing lifeboat, and missing navigation tools."),
