("char:curious|barrels", "Now, here's something most people never hear about. When the cargo was finally unloaded in Genoa, the workers counted the barrels."),
("barrels:nine", "Nine of them were empty. Out of one thousand seven hundred and one."),
("barrel:oak", "Those nine were made of red oak. Red oak is more porous than white oak, which means alcohol can slowly seep through the wood."),
("vapor:hold", "So imagine the hold. Closed up, hot from the sun, full of barrels. Some of them leaking. The air slowly filling with alcohol fumes."),
("char:scared|vapor", "Maybe the crew opened the hatch and smelled it. Strong fumes. Maybe they heard a rumble or a pop from below. On a ship packed with alcohol, that is terrifying."),
("char:shock|boom", "Captain Briggs had his wife and his little girl on board. If he believed the ship was about to explode, he'd want them off. Right now."),
("rope:tow", "Some researchers think he did something smart. He ordered everyone into the lifeboat, and kept it tied to the ship with a long rope, so they could come back once it felt safe."),
("char:think|rope", "And here's a detail that fits. When the ship was found, the peak halyard, a long heavy rope used to raise a sail, was found broken."),
("rope:snap", "So picture it. A small boat, ten people, tied to a ship by one rope. The wind picks up. The rope snaps."),
("ship:away", "And the Mary Celeste sails away from them, all by herself. Into the open Atlantic."),
("char:sad|boat", "But that's not the strangest part. The strangest part is what happened when scientists actually tested the explosion theory."),
